# Evolutionary Custom Investment Rules & Persistent Rules UI Plan

## 1. Overview & Background

The current system synthesizes candidate rules (Golden Setups and Toxic Patterns) based purely on historical realized P/L of closed round trips in [journal_analysis.py](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/services/journal_analysis.py#L939-L979) and allows users to adopt them or write manual rules in [PersonalEdgeDashboard.tsx](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/frontend/src/components/portfolio/PersonalEdgeDashboard.tsx).

However, two critical gaps remain:
1. **Lack of Rule Evolution via Journal Reviews (복기 기반 규칙 발전의 부재)**:
   - When a user logs a trade review ([review_logged_trade](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/routers/coach.py#L123-L169)) or triggers a whole journal review ([review_journal](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/routers/coach.py#L171-L198)), **existing active investment rules remain completely static and never evolve**.
   - Qualitative insights from journal entries (e.g., "FOMO dip-buying failed because 200 EMA support was not confirmed", or "Trades adhering to disciplined valuation had a 75% win rate") are not fed back into refining rule conditions, tightening risk parameters, or discovering emergent rules.
   - There is no versioning (v1, v2, v3...) or evolution history tracking how a rule changes and adapts over time.
2. **Lack of Persistent & Readily Accessible Rules UI (투자규칙 상시 조회 환경의 부재)**:
   - Users currently have to scroll all the way to the bottom of the Portfolio page to see the rules playbook under "Personal Trading Edge".
   - Users cannot easily view their established rules side-by-side while examining SEC filings, reviewing charts, or entering new trades, without constantly running or re-running full journal reviews.

This plan addresses both needs: **(1) a continuous Rule Evolution Engine** that evaluates adherence, refines conditions, and generates actionable rule evolution proposals whenever reviews are conducted, and **(2) a flexible, persistent UI** featuring an instant-access Modal, a dockable Side Drawer, and a dedicated Portfolio Screen Tab.

