#### 1. Database Schema Extension ([services/db.py](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/services/db.py))
- **`trading_rules` column additions**:
  - `version`: `INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1` (tracks rule iteration)
  - `adherence_count`: `INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0` (trades that complied with this rule)
  - `violation_count`: `INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0` (trades that breached this rule)
  - `last_evaluated_at`: `TEXT` (ISO timestamp of latest review evaluation)
  - `notes`: `TEXT` (qualitative notes or evolutionary rationale)
- **New table `rule_evolution_history`**:
  ```sql
  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS rule_evolution_history (
      id              INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
      rule_id         INTEGER NOT NULL,
      version         INTEGER NOT NULL,
      change_type     TEXT NOT NULL, -- 'created', 'condition_refined', 'stats_updated', 'risk_tightened', 'user_edited'
      trigger_source  TEXT NOT NULL, -- 'trade_review', 'journal_review', 'manual', 'edge_synthesis'
      trigger_id      INTEGER,      -- trade_id or review_id
      summary         TEXT NOT NULL, -- e.g. "Refined entry conditions after Trade #14 FOMO review"
      details_json    TEXT,         -- Before/after diff and evidence metrics
      created_at      TEXT NOT NULL,
      FOREIGN KEY (rule_id) REFERENCES trading_rules (id) ON DELETE CASCADE
  );
  ```
- **New table `rule_evolution_proposals`**:
  ```sql
  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS rule_evolution_proposals (
      id              INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
      rule_id         INTEGER,       -- null if proposing a brand new emergent rule
      proposal_type   TEXT NOT NULL, -- 'refine_existing', 'new_rule', 'tighten_risk', 'deprecate'
      rule_type       TEXT NOT NULL, -- 'golden', 'toxic', 'custom'
      title           TEXT NOT NULL,
      conditions_json TEXT NOT NULL,
      description     TEXT NOT NULL,
      rationale       TEXT NOT NULL, -- why this evolution is suggested based on the review
      evidence_review_id INTEGER,
      evidence_trade_ids TEXT,       -- JSON array of cited trade IDs
      status          TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending', -- 'pending', 'applied', 'dismissed'
      created_at      TEXT NOT NULL
  );
  ```

#### 2. Evolution Service Implementation ([services/rule_evolution.py](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/services/rule_evolution.py))
- **`evaluate_trade_against_rules(trade, review, rules)`**:
  - Compares the trade's `rationale_type`, `strategy_type`, and `emotion_tag` with active rules.
  - Computes whether the trade adhered to a Golden Rule or triggered a Toxic Pattern, updating `adherence_count` / `violation_count`.
- **`generate_evolution_proposals(reviews, trades, current_rules)`**:
  - Combines quantitative round-trip performance with LLM reflection analysis.
  - Proposes condition additions (e.g. "Only execute breakout if volume > 150%"), parameter tightening, or new emergent rules.
- **`apply_proposal(proposal_id)`**:
  - Applies proposed condition/description changes, increments rule version (`v1` → `v2`), logs the transition in `rule_evolution_history`, and marks proposal as `applied`.
- **`get_rule_history(rule_id)`**:
  - Retrieves chronological evolution audit trail for a rule.

#### 3. Agent Integration ([agents/coach_agent.py](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/agents/coach_agent.py))
- Inject active rules into `analyze_retrospective` and `analyze_journal` prompts.
- Ensure the Coach agent outputs rule adherence evaluations and evolutionary feedback.
- Automatically invoke `rule_evolution.record_review_feedback()` upon review completion.

#### 4. Coach Router Extensions ([routers/coach.py](file:///c:/Users/mrsim/FinAnalSupTool/backend/routers/coach.py))
- `GET /coach/rules/{id}/history`: Fetch version timeline for a rule.
- `GET /coach/rules/proposals`: List pending evolution proposals.
- `POST /coach/rules/proposals/generate`: On-demand trigger to analyze recent reviews and synthesize evolution proposals.
- `POST /coach/rules/proposals/{id}/apply`: Approve and apply a proposal.
- `POST /coach/rules/proposals/{id}/dismiss`: Dismiss a proposal.

